    "text": {
     "en": "Let us read and write three-digit numbers. 211 is two hundred eleven.\nTo write a number from its name, put hundreds first, then tens, then ones. Three hundred five is 305.\nFill in the missing numbers on a path: 211, 212, 213, 214, 215, 216 counting forward by one.\nCounting backward: 295, 294, 293. After 299 comes 300, so 302 and 310 follow later.\nThe expanded form splits a number: 227 is 200 + 20 + 7.\nUse a number line to place numbers like 230 between 220 and 240."
    }
